msgid "The envelope and the manifest"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*The envelope em-extension.toml key by key, with its sections data, code,"
" requires and build, and the keys of the manifest profile.json.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An archive has an **envelope** at its root, ``em-extension.toml``, "
"modelled on the manifest of Blender's extensions. It says who the archive"
" is, which EM it goes with, what it carries and what it asks. A package "
"with data has a **manifest**, ``profile.json``, which says what it adds "
"to the language. The contract behind both is `SPEC.md "
"<https://github.com/ExtendedMatrix/em-profiles/blob/main/SPEC.md>`__ of "
"em-profiles; the closed sets of values are listed, as the library reads "
"them, at the end of this page."
msgstr ""

msgid "The head"
msgstr ""

msgid "Key"
msgstr ""

msgid "Required"
msgstr ""

msgid "What it is"
msgstr ""

msgid "``schema_version``"
msgstr ""

msgid "yes"
msgstr ""

msgid "The form of the envelope: ``\"1.0.0\"``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``id``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The identity of the archive in a repository: 2 to 64 characters, "
"lowercase letters, digits, ``.``, ``_`` and ``-``, a letter or a digit "
"first. For a package with data it equals ``name`` in ``profile.json``, "
"and the folder is named after it."
msgstr ""

msgid "``version``"
msgstr ""

msgid "The version of the archive, *major.minor.patch* (see :doc:`new-version`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "``name``"
msgstr ""

msgid "The name shown in the Extensions window."
msgstr ""

msgid "``tagline``"
msgstr ""

msgid "no"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One line about it, at most 64 characters, no final full stop (a warning "
"otherwise)."
msgstr ""

msgid "``maintainer``"
msgstr ""

msgid "Who answers for the archive."
msgstr ""

msgid "``license``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A list of SPDX identifiers, each written ``\"SPDX:<id>\"``; one per "
"section when they differ."
msgstr ""

msgid "``em_api_min``, ``em_api_max``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``em_api_min``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The versions of the extensions API the archive works with: ``\"1.0\"`` "
"for data; ``\"1.2\"`` for code that stamps its files. A plugin that asks "
"for a newer API than the program's is not loaded, and the window says "
"why."
msgstr ""

msgid "``type``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``community-package``, ``plugin`` or ``mixed``; it must agree with the "
"sections. ``build`` writes it when it is missing (a warning)."
msgstr ""

msgid "An archive has at least one of the sections ``[data]`` and ``[code]``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``[data]``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``profile``"
msgstr ""

msgid "The manifest, ``\"profile.json\"``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The version of the data; by default the archive's. It equals ``version`` "
"in ``profile.json``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``root``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Where the data live: ``\".\"`` when the archive has data only, a folder "
"of their own (``\"data/\"``) when it has code too. The two roots never "
"overlap."
msgstr ""

msgid "``[[data.vocabularies]]``"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"One entry per vocabulary file the archive carries: ``path``, ``scheme`` "
"(the IRI of the ``skos:ConceptScheme`` in the file), ``version`` (its "
"``owl:versionInfo``), ``license``, ``tier`` (``fascia`` is read as the "
"same key) and ``digest`` (``\"sha256:…\"``, the fingerprint of the file)."
" A vocabulary of tier ``C`` has no ``path``: it has ``fetch = { url, "
"digest, terms }``, and the person downloads it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**No executable file lives under the data root** (the extensions are "
"listed at the end of the page); outside the roots only the envelope, "
"``LICENSE*``, ``README*`` and ``CHANGELOG.md`` may stand. This is what "
"lets the data be installed without the question of trust."
msgstr ""

msgid "``[code]``"
msgstr ""

msgid "The version of the code; by default the archive's."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Where the code lives: ``\".\"`` for a plugin alone, ``\"code/\"`` in a "
"mixed package."
msgstr ""

msgid "The licence of the code, ``\"SPDX:<id>\"``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``entry``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``\"<module>:<object>\"``: the module imported and the object whose "
"``setup(ctx)`` is called (a function ``setup`` may be named directly)."
msgstr ""

msgid "``hosts``"
msgstr ""

msgid "Where the code runs: a list of ``emstudio``, ``blender``, ``server``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``platforms``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The platforms the archive has wheels for; needed when a wheel is not pure"
" Python."
msgstr ""

msgid "``wheels``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The paths, under the code root, of the wheels of its dependencies. "
"Nothing is installed with ``pip``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``[code.permissions]``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``files``, ``network``, ``clipboard``, ``processes``: each with the "
"reason shown before installing, at most 64 characters, no final full "
"stop."
msgstr ""

msgid "``[code.descriptor]``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``capabilities`` (``read-graph`` by default; ``write-graph`` to write in "
"a study), ``host`` (``emstudio-side``), ``transport`` (``[\"direct\"]``),"
" ``provenance`` (``derivation``). For a plugin of EMStudio, "
"``capabilities`` is the key that matters."
msgstr ""

msgid "``[[code.commands]]``"
msgstr ""

msgid "The commands, below."
msgstr ""

msgid "``[[code.panels]]``"
msgstr ""

msgid "The declarative panels, below."
msgstr ""

msgid "A command, ``[[code.commands]]``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Unique in the plugin: letters, digits, ``_``, ``.`` and ``-``, a letter "
"first. ``ctx.command(id, function)`` binds it."
msgstr ""

msgid "``label``"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "A text, or one per language: ``{ en = \"…\", it = \"…\" }``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``in``"
msgstr "``w``"

msgid ""
"The slots where it appears, ``[\"menu.tools@1\"]`` (see :doc:`slots`). "
"Empty: the command exists, and is called from a panel or the console."
msgstr ""

msgid "``writes``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``true`` when it changes the study. By default ``false`` in a slot that "
"only shows (a check, a section, a column, the status bar, a layer), "
"``true`` elsewhere."
msgstr ""

msgid "``slots``"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"What it receives: ``[{ name = \"…\", kind = \"…\", required = false }]``."
" The kinds are listed at the end of the page; a slot is required unless "
"``required = false``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``when``"
msgstr "``kiedy``"

msgid ""
"When it is offered, in a small closed grammar: ``document`` (a study is "
"open), ``selection:none|any|one|many``, ``selection:US|USV`` (every "
"selected node of these types), joined by ``and``. Empty: always."
msgstr ""

msgid "``accept``, ``claims``, ``folders``, ``panel``"
msgstr ""

msgid "For a reader of **Bring in…** (``door.reader@2``), see :doc:`slots`."
msgstr ""

msgid "``primitive``, ``icon``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For a tool of the Space (``space.tool@1``): what the person places, and "
"one or two characters drawn on the button."
msgstr ""

msgid "``view``"
msgstr ""

msgid "For a column of the Tabular window: the sheet it joins."
msgstr ""

msgid "``layer``"
msgstr ""

msgid "For a layer of the Space: ``raster_stack``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``buttons``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For a section of the Inspector: ids of commands of the same plugin, drawn"
" as buttons under the rows."
msgstr ""

msgid "A panel, ``[[code.panels]]``"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A panel is a few fields drawn by EMStudio, never HTML: ``id``, ``label``,"
" ``place`` (where it opens the first time), ``when``, and "
"``[[code.panels.fields]]``. A field has a ``kind``: ``text``, ``number`` "
"(with ``unit``, ``min``, ``max``, ``step``), ``choice`` (with "
"``options``, each ``{ value, label }``), ``check``, ``node`` — what the "
"person fills, with a ``name``: the slot of the same name of the command a"
" button runs — or ``value`` (a read-only command whose answer is shown) "
"and ``button`` (a command run with the fields), both with ``command``. "
"Every field may have ``label`` and ``help``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``[requires]``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Version ranges are those of npm and Blender: ``^``, ``~``, ``>=``/``<``, "
"``=``, ``*``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``part`` says which section of the other archive is needed: ``data``, "
"``code`` or ``any``. Data never require code as a must: a dependency with"
" ``part = \"code\"`` is always ``optional = true``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A package whose mandatory dependency is missing is installed all the "
"same, shown as incomplete, and its data stay readable. A repository "
"installs the dependencies first."
msgstr ""

msgid "``[build]``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``paths`` (the files and folders to put in the archive) and "
"``paths_exclude_pattern`` (what to leave out; ``__pycache__/`` and "
"``*.pyc`` by default), as in Blender."
msgstr ""

msgid "The manifest, ``profile.json``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``profile_format``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``\"0.2\"``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``iri``, ``name``, ``prefix``, ``version``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The identity: the address, the name (= the id), the prefix of every type "
"(2 to 16 lowercase letters or digits, a letter first), the version of the"
" data."
msgstr ""

msgid "``lifecycle``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``proposed``, ``stable`` or ``deprecated``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``title``, ``description``"
msgstr ""

msgid "Texts per language."
msgstr ""

msgid "``languages``, ``unverified_languages``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The languages of the package (a label is required in each, for every "
"type), and those no person has reviewed yet."
msgstr ""

msgid "``curators``, ``license``, ``parts``"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Who answers for it; the licence of the content, an SPDX identifier; "
"another licence for a file or a folder (``\"examples/\": {\"license\": "
"\"CC0-1.0\"}``)."
msgstr ""

msgid "``is_profile_of``"
msgstr ""

msgid "The versions of the em.json format and of the EM core it was written for."
msgstr ""

msgid "``datamodel_checked``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The versions of the core's datamodels it was checked against; never a "
"reason to refuse."
msgstr ""

msgid "``requires``"
msgstr ""

msgid "Copied from the envelope's ``[requires]`` by ``build``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``qualia_vocabularies``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A property bound to a SKOS scheme: ``property_type``, ``label``, "
"``scheme``, ``version``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``qualia``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The package's own properties: ``id``, ``label``, ``data_type`` "
"(``float``, ``integer``, ``string``, ``boolean``, ``date``, "
"``controlled_vocabulary``), ``units``, ``mapping``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``extractor_types``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Kinds of reading: ``id``, ``specializes`` (``extractor``), ``label``, "
"``geometry`` (``primitive``, ``produces``, ``unit``, ``vertices``, "
"``snap``: ``surface``/``vertex``/``free``, ``frame``: "
"``model``/``graph``), ``produces``, ``source_documents``, "
"``input_formats``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``landmark_sets``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Sets of points: ``id``, ``path`` (``landmarks/<id>.json``), "
"``extractor_type``, ``label``. The file lists ``points``, each with "
"``id``, ``concept``, ``required``, ``side``, ``mirror``, ``ref``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``combiner_types``"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Computations: ``id``, ``label``, ``operation``, ``inputs`` "
"(``{\"landmark\": \"<set>/<point>\"}`` or ``{\"quale\": \"…\"}``), "
"``produces``, ``unit``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``document_types``, ``file_types``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Documents of the community (``specializes``: ``document``, "
"``content_nature``, ``formats``) and file types with their ``reader`` "
"(``builtin:<id>`` or ``plugin:<id>``)."
msgstr ""

msgid "``forms``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Recording sheets: ``id``, ``source`` (``template.yaml``), ``compiled``, "
"``digest``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``color_schemes``, ``visual_rules``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Colour schemes (``id``, ``path`` of an ``.emc``, ``property``, ``label``)"
" and how the package's types are drawn."
msgstr ""

msgid "``i18n``, ``help``, ``examples``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Interface strings per language, help pages, and at least one example "
"study."
msgstr ""

msgid "``node_types``, ``edge_types``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Suspended in EM 1.6: accepted with a warning in a ``proposed`` package, "
"refused in a ``stable`` one (see :doc:`design`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The closed sets"
msgstr ""

msgid "Values"
msgstr ""

msgid "``[code].permissions``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``files``, ``network``, ``clipboard``, ``processes``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``[code].hosts``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``emstudio``, ``blender``, ``server``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``[code].platforms``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``macos-arm64``, ``macos-x64``, ``windows-x64``, ``windows-arm64``, "
"``linux-x64``, ``linux-arm64``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``[code.descriptor].capabilities``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``read-graph``, ``write-graph``, ``subscribe``, ``link-selection``, "
"``presence``, ``attach-asset``, ``resolve-asset``, ``resolve-preview``, "
"``materialize-3D``, ``publish-3D``, ``ingest-batch``, ``resolve-uri``"
msgstr ""

msgid "capabilities that write"
msgstr ""

msgid "``write-graph``, ``attach-asset``, ``materialize-3D``, ``ingest-batch``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``kind`` of a slot of a command"
msgstr ""

msgid "``id``, ``ids``, ``string``, ``number``, ``path``, ``geometry``, ``bool``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``when``, the selection"
msgstr ""

msgid "``none``, ``any``, ``one``, ``many``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``primitive`` of a tool of the Space"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``point`` (1 click), ``line`` (2 clicks), ``polyline`` (2+ clicks), "
"``surface`` (3+ clicks)"
msgstr ""

msgid "``view`` of a column of the Tabular"
msgstr ""

msgid "``Units``, ``Epochs``, ``Documents``, ``Claims``, ``Authors``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``layer`` of a layer of the Space"
msgstr ""

msgid "``raster_stack``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``kind`` of a field of a panel"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``number``, ``text``, ``choice``, ``node``, ``check``, ``value``, "
"``button``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``place`` of a panel"
msgstr ""

msgid "``right``, ``left``, ``below``, ``window``"
msgstr ""

msgid "fields of a panel, at most"
msgstr ""

msgid "40"
msgstr ""

msgid "``geometry.primitive`` of an extractor → ``produces``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``point`` → ``position``, ``elevation``, ``line`` → ``length``, "
"``polyline`` → ``length``, ``surface`` → ``area``, ``volume`` → "
"``volume``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``operation`` of a combiner"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``distance`` (2 landmarks), ``angle`` (3 landmarks), ``ratio`` (2 "
"qualia), ``mean`` (1+ inputs), ``area_of_polygon`` (3+ landmarks), "
"``elevation_difference`` (2 landmarks), ``angle_between_planes`` (6 "
"landmarks), ``symmetry_index`` (2+ landmarks)"
msgstr ""

msgid "``reader`` of a file type, ``builtin:<id>``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``gltf``, ``glb``, ``mesh``, ``pointcloud``, ``image``, ``pdf``, ``3tz``,"
" ``iiif``, ``text``, ``svg``, ``video``, ``audio``"
msgstr ""

msgid "files never under the data root"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``.py``, ``.pyc``, ``.pyo``, ``.so``, ``.dylib``, ``.dll``, ``.js``, "
"``.mjs``, ``.wasm``, ``.whl``, ``.exe``"
msgstr ""

